    "updated_at": "2026-11-12T01:32:57Z",
    "body": "Part 1 (re-pin for the cut) on issue/980-bore-pin · PR #1003 (draft, head 2c97351b) · pinned by `pocket3d_hsm::the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean` · merges when reviewed. Test-only, `Refs #980`: this issue stays open for part 2.\n\nMeasured with the test itself (release, `--ignored`):\n| Commit | Result | Rings levels | moves / planar / arcs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 575f02d8^1 (3bd54fc9) | pass | Z 20 | 5530 / 5497 / 600 |\n| 575f02d8 (PR #839 merge) | fail line 100 | Z 20 (-1.66, -2.80), Z 10 (-1.99, -0.13) | 6500 / 6464 / 222 |\n| f490458a (main) | fail line 100 | same | 6500 / 6464 / 222 |\n\nCause confirmed: #839's 0.005 mm STEP chord cap meshes the bore much finer; on the new outline the Z 10 HSM plan crosses itself and the planner refuses it (rings cut it, named in the notes). Warnings empty at all three. Also seen: the HSM levels now fit 80 arcs each (was 173-284), so arcs fall 600 -> 222. The re-pinned test is green 3 times on the branch with identical numbers (deterministic). Every safety assertion is unchanged.\n\nFor part 2: the Z 20 crossing point moved too ((-2.33, -2.78) -> (-1.66, -2.80)), and Z 15/5 still plan - so it's level-specific, which suggests looking at the Z 10 slice of the finer mesh (near-duplicate vertices or a sliver) before the planner. The motion crate's debug twin did not see this because it plans a hand-built 256-gon bore, not the STEP import.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
    "pin": null,
