    "body": "PR #1003 merged as part 1 (`Refs #980`): the heavy pin is re-measured for the 0.18.0 cut (levels Z 20 and Z 10 fall back to Offset rings; 6500 moves / 6464 planar feeds / 222 arcs), every safety assertion unchanged. This issue stays open for part 2: get the Z 10 level's HSM plan back on the finer STEP mesh of #839, or record why it cannot be. Reviewer's open point for part 2: the verify laws prove no gouge, they do not prove the rings level clears the stock as fully as the HSM plan did - check rest material on that level. `in-review` removed (no open PR).",
