    "created_at": "2026-11-12T03:33:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-12T03:33:28Z",
    "body": "fix on issue/980-bore-hsm-plan · PR #1032 · pinned by `motion adaptive_orbit_seam::the_users_z10_bore_level_keeps_its_hsm_plan`, `rings::tests::the_orbit_closes_on_its_own_start_and_the_spiral_leaves_it_uncrossed`, heavy `pocket3d_hsm::the_users_bore_roughs_adaptive_level_by_level_and_verifies_clean` · merges when reviewed\n\nCause (from a dump of the Z 10 level's center area and plan): not the mesh. The plan's \"crossing\" is segment 0 (the entry orbit's first chord) against segment 96 (the spiral's first chord out of the orbit's closing vertex); `adaptive::rings::circle` put that closing vertex at `a0 + TAU`, 7.7e-16 mm off the start, and the orientation predicate read the ulp as a proper crossing. Z 20's fallback (since #850) is the same seam. #839's finer mesh only changed which levels the float noise hit.\n\nFix: the circle closes exactly on its start (snap within 1e-9 mm); the crossing law is unchanged. Heavy pin, three release runs, identical: no level falls back, verifies clean, 16197 moves / 15458 planar / 1581 arcs. Part 1's open point (rest material on a rings level) is moot: no level of the bore falls back now.\n",
    "author_association": "OWNER",
